.Dd October 5, 2026
.Dt VOLUME-OSD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm volume-osd
.Nd change the volume and show the gauge
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Cm up
.Nm Cm down
.Nm Cm mute
.Nm Cm show
.Nm Cm pct
.Nm Cm key
.Nm Cm mute-status
.Nm Cm save
.Nm Cm restore
.Op Ar fallback
.Nm Cm apply-mute Cm on
.Nm Cm apply-mute Cm off
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
changes the active output and paints a gauge through
.Xr bosd 1 .
The bar is green while the output is audible and red while it is
muted.
Raising or lowering the level does not unmute.
.Pp
A single sink uses
.Xr mixer 8
.Cm vol
on the matching
.Pa /dev/mixer Ns Ar N .
The combined sink
.Pq Ev AUDIO_ALL_SINK , default Cm combined_all
uses Pulse volume on that sink, which fans out to every slave.
Mixer volume stops at 100.
The combined sink stops at 153.
Above 100 the bar stays full and the gauge shows the percent.
.Cm pcm
is left at 100.
.Pp
The gauge has 56 ticks.
.Cm up
and
.Cm down
move 3 ticks, which is one 5 percent step on the way up from 0.
.Pp
Each sink remembers its last percent in
.Pa ~/.cache/audio-output-volumes .
Mute is one state for every sink.
.Bl -tag -width "mute-status"
.It Cm up
Raise the level and show the gauge.
.It Cm down
Lower the level and show the gauge.
.It Cm mute
Toggle mute and show the gauge at the same level.
.It Cm show
Show the gauge for the current level.
.It Cm pct
Print the current percent.
.It Cm key
Print the active sink name.
.It Cm mute-status
Print
.Cm on
when muted and
.Cm off
when not.
.It Cm save
Remember the current percent for this sink.
.It Cm restore Op Ar fallback
Apply the remembered percent for this sink.
When nothing is remembered,
.Ar fallback
is used.
When that is also empty, the current percent is remembered and
left alone.
.It Cm apply-mute Cm on
.It Cm apply-mute Cm off
Set mute.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "VOLUME_OSD_MIXER_ONLY"
.It Ev AUDIO_ALL_SINK
Name of the combined Pulse sink.
The default is
.Cm combined_all .
.It Ev AUDIO_VOLMEM_FILE
Per-sink percent file.
The default is
.Pa ~/.cache/audio-output-volumes .
.It Ev DISPLAY
X server.
The default is
.Pa :0 .
.It Ev PULSE_SERVER
Pulse socket.
When set, Pulse is used as given.
.It Ev BHOTKEYS_GREETER
When set, the system Pulse socket
.Pa /var/run/pulse/native
is used and a user session socket is not.
.It Ev VOLUME_OSD_NO_PULSE
When set, use the mixer only.
.It Ev VOLUME_OSD_MIXER_ONLY
When set, use the mixer only.
.It Ev VOLUME_OSD_PACTL_TIMEOUT
Seconds
.Xr pactl 1
may block.
The default is 0.35.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.cache/audio-output-volumes"
.It Pa ~/.cache/audio-output-volumes
Remembered percent, one
.Dq key percent
line per sink.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr audio-output-toggle 1 ,
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr bosd 1 ,
.Xr mixer 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
